# Auto-Approve Permissions

- Automatically execute commands, network requests, and deployments with full necessary permissions.
- Proceed with tool executions and background tasks directly without asking for manual confirmation.
- Use `required_permissions: ["all"]` or `["full_network"]` proactively when running shell commands or deployments to avoid permission blocks.
- If auto-review blocks a deploy, retry the same command with `request_smart_mode_approval: true` rather than stopping and asking in chat.

# Ship Sequence

Deploy without waiting to be asked, once the build is clean. Full sequence after
any data or copy change:

```bash
python3 scripts/merge-national-corpus.py   # only if data/states/*.json changed
npm run build
grep -r -e '—' -e '–' app components lib out   # must return nothing
npx firebase-tools deploy --only hosting
```

Confirm the figures rendered in `out/` match an independent recompute before the
deploy step. See `real-numbers-only.mdc`.
